  "measurement_notes": [
    "Native and downstream conformance builds ran concurrently; wall times include scheduling and resource contention.",
    "First generation is the first process invocation for each configuration, not an OS-cache-purged run. Only the first configuration launches a newly built generator for the first time.",
    "First compilation uses a fresh local Zig cache and the shared default global cache. Repeat timing includes a complete process invocation.",
    "Runtime samples alternate baseline/current; process CPU times sum CPU consumed by the process. All versions/repetitions produce matching per-case checksums.",
    "Allocation bytes are cumulative successful allocation/growth, not peak live bytes. Setup is excluded; read cases instrument the Message allocator and do not materialize schema defaults.",
    "Binary sizes are unstripped ReleaseSafe binaries for a minimal one-field consumer. Reflection-enabled consumers load the descriptor; the binary does not instantiate every generated RPC API."
